Step 2: replace INVOICE_ID. Webhooks follow within a few seconds.
Anyone who opens a test invoice's checkout page can pay it there with pretend money. Remove "test": true before you go live, and never ship an order for a test invoice: act only on webhooks, or GET responses, with "livemode": true.
| scenario | What happens | Result
| detected | The full amount is seen on the network but not yet confirmed. | pending (webhook invoice.pending)
| confirm | Confirms everything seen so far. Run it after "detected". | paid if the amount was enough
| exact | The exact amount arrives with all confirmations. | paid
| underpaid_1pct | 1% less than the amount due arrives. | paid, flag underpaidWithinTolerance (inside the default 1% tolerance). With a store tolerance below 1%: nothing changes and the response has "radar": true.
| underpaid_5pct | 5% less than the amount due arrives. | Fixed address (the default): outside the tolerance, so nothing changes and the response has "radar": true. Older invoices with their own address: paid_partial.
| overpaid | 2% more than the amount due arrives. | More than the default 1% tolerance, so it is not paid by itself. Fixed address (the default): nothing changes and the response has "radar": true. Invoices with their own address: status pending and the event invoice.needs_review. With a store tolerance of 2% or more: paid, flag overpaid.
| partial_half | Half the amount arrives. | Fixed address (the default): nothing changes and the response has "radar": true. Older invoices with their own address: paid_partial.
| late | The invoice is moved past its expiry, then the full amount arrives. | paid, flag late

### What we send
Each webhook is a JSON POST to your store's webhook URL with these headers:
- ArionPay-Event: one of invoice.pending, invoice.partial, invoice.paid, invoice.expired or invoice.needs_review.
- ArionPay-Event-Id: a unique ID. Store it and ignore repeats.
- ArionPay-Signature: t=<timestamp>,v1=<hex>, where v1 is the HMAC-SHA256 of <timestamp>.<raw body> signed with your store's webhook secret.
### Before you fulfil an order
- Compute the signature from the raw request body and compare it in constant time.
- Reject old timestamps (we suggest more than 5 minutes).
- Use the event ID so a repeated delivery doesn't ship an order twice.
- Find the order by data.invoice.id (saved when you created the invoice) and check amountFiat and currency.
- Answer with a 2xx status within 10 seconds. Other answers, redirects and timeouts are retried for about 3 days.
Webhooks from test invoices are marked as test (livemode: false). In production, act only on livemode: true. The webhook secret (whsec_…) is not your API secret: you get it on the Webhooks page with "Replace secret".
```
// Node.js
const crypto = require('crypto');

// rawBody: the request body exactly as received (a string), before any JSON parsing
function verifyArionPayWebhook(rawBody, header, secret, toleranceSec = 300) {
  const parts = Object.fromEntries(header.split(',').map((p) => p.trim().split('=')));
  const ts = parts.t || '';
  const given = parts.v1 || '';
  if (!/^\d+$/.test(ts) || Math.abs(Date.now() / 1000 - Number(ts)) > toleranceSec) return false;
  if (!/^[0-9a-f]{64}$/.test(given)) return false;
  const expected = crypto
.createHmac('sha256', secret)
.update(`${ts}.${rawBody}`)
.digest();
  return crypto.timingSafeEqual(expected, Buffer.from(given, 'hex'));
}
```
